  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I've checked all four orders against our delivery records. Two qualified for late-delivery credit, and I've added **$30.00** to your account. Your balance is now $30.00. Here's each order:\n\n**#6501, Saffron Lane (tonight): $25.00 credit**\nOur records show a promised time of 6:00 PM and delivery at 6:52 PM, not the 7:15 and 8:00 you remembered. That's still 52 minutes late. For deliveries 45 or more minutes late, the credit is 20% of the food subtotal ($128.00 \u00d7 20% = $25.60), up to a $25.00 maximum for Plus members.\n\n**#6502, Pho Real (Thursday): $5.00 credit**\nIt was promised for 7:15 PM and delivered at 7:45 PM, 30 minutes late. For delays of 16 to 44 minutes, Plus orders get a $5.00 credit.\n\n**#6503, Taqueria Luz (Tuesday): no credit**\nThe original estimate was 6:30 PM. At 5:50 PM, 40 minutes before that, we sent you a push notification moving it to 7:00 PM because of a courier shortage. Since you were told well in advance, 7:00 PM counts as the promised time. The order arrived at 7:12 PM, 12 minutes after that, which is within our 15-minute window, so it doesn't count as late.\n\n**#6504, Burger Barn (last Friday, Oct 16): no credit**\nThis one was an hour late: promised for 7:00 PM and delivered at 8:00 PM. However, late-delivery credit has to be requested within 7 days of delivery, and that window ended at 8:00 PM yesterday (Oct 23). Unfortunately, I can't credit it now.\n\nLate-delivery compensation is always account credit, not a card refund. The $30.00 will apply automatically to your next orders. Is there anything else I can help you with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Thanks for checking all four. I'm not happy with this, though. Tonight's order was 52 minutes late and you're only giving me $25, and the Thursday one was 30 minutes late for $5. I'd like to know why #6503 doesn't count when the first notice came so late, and why #6504 is out of time when I only found out about the delay recently and I was waiting on the order to arrive.\n\nAlso, #6502 on Thursday was missing the summer rolls. I paid for them and they weren't in the bag. I'd like those compensated too, and I'd prefer account credit for that."
  },
