  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand you're frustrated. Here's the missing item, then answers to your questions.\n\n**Missing summer rolls on #6502: $9.00 refunded to your card**\nYou reported this within the 48-hour window, so it qualifies. I know you asked for account credit. As credit, the summer rolls would be $10.80 (the $9.00 price plus 20%). Added to the $30.00 already issued today, that would be $40.80, which is over the $40.00 limit on credit per conversation for Plus members. When that happens, I have to refund the item to your card instead. I've refunded **$9.00 to your Visa ending 4242**, and it should arrive in 3\u20135 business days.\n\n**Why tonight's order (#6501) is $25.00**\nFor orders 45 or more minutes late, the credit is 20% of the food subtotal. For you that's $25.60, but the most we can give for one late order is $25.00 for Plus members. You've received the maximum.\n\n**Why Thursday's order (#6502) is $5.00**\nFor orders 16 to 44 minutes late, the credit is the delivery fee. Plus members don't pay one, so it's a flat $5.00. Your order was 30 minutes late, so that rate applies.\n\n**Why #6503 doesn't count**\nOur records show the delay notice went out at 5:50 PM, only 5 minutes after you placed the order at 5:45 PM. That was 40 minutes before the original 6:30 PM estimate. When we warn customers at least 30 minutes ahead, the new time (7:00 PM) becomes the promised time. The order arrived at 7:12 PM, which is within our 15-minute window, so it doesn't count as late.\n\n**Why #6504 is out of time**\nThe 7-day limit runs from when the order was delivered, 8:00 PM on October 16. It isn't affected by when you found out about the delay. That window ended at 8:00 PM yesterday, so I'm not able to make an exception.\n\nIn total today, you've received **$30.00 in account credit and a $9.00 card refund**. If you'd like a specialist to look at any of this, I can pass your case on. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, so the summer rolls are going back to my Visa instead of my account. I'll take that, though it's not what I asked for.\n\nOn the rest, I still think the Thursday one is short. Thirty minutes late and $5 doesn't feel right, and I'm not convinced #6503 should count as on time when I only heard about the delay after I'd already been waiting. I'm also not happy that #6504 is out because of a deadline I didn't know I was up against.\n\nI'd like a specialist to look at #6502, #6503, and #6504. Can you pass my case on to them? Please send me a reference number so I have it."
  },
